<title>SINGAPORE: Lim Kah Ngam gets redevelopment go-ahead.</title>
<headline>Lim Kah Ngam gets redevelopment go-ahead.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Property and construction company Lim Kah Ngam Ltd said on Thursday it had won permission from Singapore's Urban Redevelopment Authority (URA) to redevelop its Hotel Equatorial into condominium housing.</p>
<p>It said in a statement it received a notice of provisional permission from the URA with an approved plot ratio of 2.1 for the condominium.</p>
<p>This means the condomium project would be able to have a total gross floor area twice that of the land area.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
